    "result_text": "All 257 tests pass. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `registrationDate` behavior on `POST /api/owners` \u2014 when no registration date is supplied it defaults to the server's current date, and the value is returned as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, it flows into both the input DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and the output DTO (`OwnerDto`). `format: date` generates a `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`) field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with getter/setter.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after mapping the request, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when it's null; a supplied date is preserved.\n- **Schema DDL** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\nMapStruct maps the matching `registrationDate` field automatically in both directions, so no mapper change was needed. Tests use the hsqldb profile; both new acceptance tests (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) and the full 257-test suite pass.",
